From 12cd1b1f492186f4aad05e07d8237209982eafb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 16:29:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/40] SF: gate the ARC dialog input-frame strip on the
 metadata VALUE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

fillInputFrameInfo strips the translation from layerToScreen so a
floating-activity modal or whole-task dialog gets an input frame at the
screen origin, matching the modal window's buffer origin. It was gated on
metadata.has(METADATA_IS_DIALOG), which tests PRESENCE — but WM stamps
IS_DIALOG on every task layer, carrying 0 for an ordinary app, and
children inherit the key. So the strip fired for every non-trusted layer
of every task.

That stayed hidden because a task's own activity layer sits at the VD
origin (base 0042 puts the task origin at 0,0), where the strip is a
no-op. A task SUB-window is not at the origin. YouTube's
quality/playback-speed PopupWindow drew at pos=(1314,95) while its input
frame was moved to (0,0): the panel rendered perfectly and was completely
untappable. Any offset sub-window — overflow menu, dropdown, spinner — was
affected the same way.

Test the value instead. Real dialogs and floating activities carry 1 and
still strip.

Verified on device, both directions:
  - popup input frame [1109,0][1600,494] (origin) -> [1014,1314][1505,1808]
    (its real position, physical coords on the ROT_90 panel), and the panel
    is clickable again;
  - the time-picker AlertDialog's floating modal still strips, input frame
    [821,0][1600,576], and CANCEL still dismisses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I6c94aa52ba24eb5bed66b47330e5ebb7dd4d0da2
---
 services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
index 9946e525a8..6f20923f70 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
@@ -2487,9 +2487,20 @@ void Layer::fillInputFrameInfo(WindowInfo& info, const ui::Transform& screenToDi
     // !isTrustedOverlay() to strip only the dialog card (the activity content),
     // never the task caption/decor trusted overlays — stripping those would move
     // their touchable regions over the card.
-    if (mDrawingState.metadata.has(METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY)
-            || (mDrawingState.metadata.has(METADATA_IS_DIALOG)
-                    && !isTrustedOverlay())) {
+    //
+    // Test the VALUE, not mere presence: WM stamps IS_DIALOG on every task layer,
+    // carrying 0 for an ordinary app, and children inherit the key. Keying on
+    // has() therefore stripped the translation off every non-trusted layer of
+    // every task. That went unnoticed because a task's own activity layer sits at
+    // the VD origin, where the strip is a no-op — but a task SUB-window does not.
+    // A PopupWindow (YouTube's quality/playback-speed panel, pos=(1314,95)) had
+    // its input frame moved to (0,0) while it kept drawing at its real offset, so
+    // it rendered correctly and was completely untappable.
+    const bool isFloatingActivityLayer =
+            mDrawingState.metadata.getInt32(METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY, 0) != 0;
+    const bool isDialogTaskLayer =
+            mDrawingState.metadata.getInt32(METADATA_IS_DIALOG, 0) != 0;
+    if (isFloatingActivityLayer || (isDialogTaskLayer && !isTrustedOverlay())) {
         const Rect screenRect{layerToScreen.transform(croppedInsetBoundsInLayer)};
         ui::Transform originShift;
         originShift.set(static_cast<float>(-screenRect.left),
-- 
